    <notes>
        <note id="8">Just a point of order here, but in Tales of Symphonia the world they inhabit is not known as Earth. Raine would consider "Earth" as just the element itself and "ruins of Earth" as the Earth Temple. The actual name of the world is going to be Aselia in some several thousands years, but in Raine's time the world has only just been reunited from its two halves: Sylvarant and Tethe'alla. The two halves of the combined world are still referred to by their separate names. Maybe you were (to some degree) aware of all this, but I just wanted to bring it up in case you were hoping this line of questioning would go in a different direction.</note>
